[{:db/id "q-42153/selection/71bba66f601af80429ccf164a86d99649addfac65d7789b91a307959c1dbcb5d" :answer/id #uuid "d17a02a7-dc78-59ce-b854-4e616189baa5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2-3y \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-42153/selection/577ff51810dca35e8fdee9ac113d8c65a1523b238a5b84cd940a2adb1de065de" :answer/id #uuid "7fa24236-4a87-5b19-82dc-1b1593ea610e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1-3y \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-42153/selection/842fbd156ca8305686f6743a65223e15155ae7331655dc0ca431c9478a06bcc2" :answer/id #uuid "f677cbb4-ef6d-5c06-b7e8-343fba1061ce" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2+3y \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-42153/selection/6d6811ceb4fb69a54ce1b24e6804e5f0148bafa1b76b847b06436eb966d36b67" :answer/id #uuid "d1edcbbb-9d9a-5ad0-bde3-3fde951d4a94" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "No solution" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-42153/selection/8c5f47bd701060728ec03057018baf6ac27f29282329f8c459c6a04aad71eb00" :answer/id #uuid "3ebc0ac4-f033-51b8-9432-f4e3f0ff5e56" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1+3y \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-42153/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "639420bc-b662-5eef-8212-3d10fa1e9bbb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-42153/selection/71bba66f601af80429ccf164a86d99649addfac65d7789b91a307959c1dbcb5d" :answer-field/choices ["q-42153/selection/71bba66f601af80429ccf164a86d99649addfac65d7789b91a307959c1dbcb5d" "q-42153/selection/577ff51810dca35e8fdee9ac113d8c65a1523b238a5b84cd940a2adb1de065de" "q-42153/selection/842fbd156ca8305686f6743a65223e15155ae7331655dc0ca431c9478a06bcc2" "q-42153/selection/6d6811ceb4fb69a54ce1b24e6804e5f0148bafa1b76b847b06436eb966d36b67" "q-42153/selection/8c5f47bd701060728ec03057018baf6ac27f29282329f8c459c6a04aad71eb00"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-42153" :question/id #uuid "653d2739-ff74-51ff-bc93-114e79b1a15b" :question/math-academy-id "q-42153" :question/problem "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x+3y=2 \\\\ 3x+9y=6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form, and then find the general solution of the linear system." :question/worked-solution "First, we set up the augmented matrix for the system:\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 9 & 6\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nReducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 9 & 6\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x+3y=2 \\\\ 0x+0y=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince any pair of numbers $x,y$ is a solution of the final equation $0x+0y=0,$ we can remove this equation from the system. So, our system now consists of a single equation\n\n$$\nx+3y=2.\n$$\n\nThe first variable $(x)$ is the basic variable, and the second variable $(y)$ is the free variable. Solving for the basic variable $(x)$ in terms of the free variable $(y),$ we get $x=2-3y,$ and the general solution is\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=2-3y \\\\ y=y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $y$ is an arbitrary number. \n\nIn vector form, the general solution can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2-3y \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-42153/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "07f2ae4c-ff07-5b99-a7b0-90f460081eef"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-42153"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} [:db/retract 17592186106241 :question/answer-fields 17592186103955] {:db/id "q-42155/selection/ma-v1/cf196ad86b3a87084678e924abd0f5083f889607f658b12f78f9abefafbdc22f/c7b7707c2342d102fda579fdc234a9a2a665c1280bdad92adbbe78ed4f27d5de" :answer/id #uuid "54704bdc-c31c-59d0-b581-56b96711eb09" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}3+y \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-42155/selection/ma-v1/cf196ad86b3a87084678e924abd0f5083f889607f658b12f78f9abefafbdc22f/e21aab16ffcaaacee4a0a1e37529d08d2975baab11334207427476d0f21d9694" :answer/id #uuid "63c74d62-cd4c-5afe-84e2-57a8b7aced67" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}3-y \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-42155/selection/ma-v1/cf196ad86b3a87084678e924abd0f5083f889607f658b12f78f9abefafbdc22f/1dec0728d1c22960bac5c70889e8ae33ef97ffb688ad52b2bfd435a7275927ac" :answer/id #uuid "11c48728-7b02-57ec-ba2b-49ae0c32c250" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-3+y \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-42155/selection/ma-v1/cf196ad86b3a87084678e924abd0f5083f889607f658b12f78f9abefafbdc22f/53a6b78203df5ea597ce375449ae47ac3f004975b2675fcad45f8de35480428e" :answer/id #uuid "f44fbff9-976f-5fcc-8423-4607a07508e5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-3-y \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-42155/selection/ma-v1/cf196ad86b3a87084678e924abd0f5083f889607f658b12f78f9abefafbdc22f/3e2593cf09a4e57cc7df3ae6b7abf61c18b5da3b74fd776c0d3a7337a311f36c" :answer/id #uuid "0500f257-a8cd-568a-9bc4-5657a1262a10" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1+y \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-42155/selection/ma-v1/cf196ad86b3a87084678e924abd0f5083f889607f658b12f78f9abefafbdc22f" :answer-field/id #uuid "36f5e20a-48c7-5cad-8cfd-89381794a4ff" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-42155/selection/ma-v1/cf196ad86b3a87084678e924abd0f5083f889607f658b12f78f9abefafbdc22f/c7b7707c2342d102fda579fdc234a9a2a665c1280bdad92adbbe78ed4f27d5de" :answer-field/choices ["q-42155/selection/ma-v1/cf196ad86b3a87084678e924abd0f5083f889607f658b12f78f9abefafbdc22f/c7b7707c2342d102fda579fdc234a9a2a665c1280bdad92adbbe78ed4f27d5de" "q-42155/selection/ma-v1/cf196ad86b3a87084678e924abd0f5083f889607f658b12f78f9abefafbdc22f/e21aab16ffcaaacee4a0a1e37529d08d2975baab11334207427476d0f21d9694" "q-42155/selection/ma-v1/cf196ad86b3a87084678e924abd0f5083f889607f658b12f78f9abefafbdc22f/1dec0728d1c22960bac5c70889e8ae33ef97ffb688ad52b2bfd435a7275927ac" "q-42155/selection/ma-v1/cf196ad86b3a87084678e924abd0f5083f889607f658b12f78f9abefafbdc22f/53a6b78203df5ea597ce375449ae47ac3f004975b2675fcad45f8de35480428e" "q-42155/selection/ma-v1/cf196ad86b3a87084678e924abd0f5083f889607f658b12f78f9abefafbdc22f/3e2593cf09a4e57cc7df3ae6b7abf61c18b5da3b74fd776c0d3a7337a311f36c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-42155"] :question/problem "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by \n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 3 \\\\ -3 & 3 & -9\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce $M$ to row echelon form, and then find the general solution of the linear system represented by the matrix." :question/worked-solution "Reducing $M$ to echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 3 \\\\ -3 & 3 & -9\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x-y=3 \\\\ 0x+0y=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince any pair of numbers $x,y$ is a solution of the final equation $0x+0y=0,$ we can remove this equation from the system. So, our system now consists of a single equation\n\n$$\nx-y=3.\n$$\n\nThe first variable $(x)$ is the basic variable, and the second variable $(y)$ is the free variable. Solving for the basic variable $(x)$ in terms of the free variable $(y),$ we get $x=3+y,$ and the general solution is\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=3+y \\\\ y=y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $y$ is an arbitrary number. \n\nIn vector form, the general solution can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}3+y \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-42155/selection/ma-v1/cf196ad86b3a87084678e924abd0f5083f889607f658b12f78f9abefafbdc22f"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-73751/selection/ea52913caa60331a7bd0852d4e4787a8445e911dd3d21a0c44e83537268be5c2" :answer/id #uuid "137e4fc9-3cf1-5aad-abee-06f6bea29842" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-2+y \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73751/selection/6d6811ceb4fb69a54ce1b24e6804e5f0148bafa1b76b847b06436eb966d36b67" :answer/id #uuid "71985084-024d-5240-8df3-c775e8ff5571" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "No solution" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73751/selection/985f6b5ef1c8517ebf2244547e58da77a03c4a2e843c87009b203c6ea3c30ce0" :answer/id #uuid "bfa1ce79-3c94-5097-8c92-c5a09759b978" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-1+2y \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73751/selection/c16f73c6dcd2feff45d079ef404d7c8b47cf8f04221ee0cbcf38ede15c995ec9" :answer/id #uuid "690d484c-33f3-5456-bbd8-4cedbabc9223" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2-y \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73751/selection/b281b0c65b28852a265e45d86efbe0f872541b03035b263e65e84f5f30e8f7a0" :answer/id #uuid "4e61db4d-def4-5548-80af-8e2f6152eb51" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1-2y \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73751/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "599d4de6-db25-5015-aab3-2ab595339a3a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-73751/selection/6d6811ceb4fb69a54ce1b24e6804e5f0148bafa1b76b847b06436eb966d36b67" :answer-field/choices ["q-73751/selection/ea52913caa60331a7bd0852d4e4787a8445e911dd3d21a0c44e83537268be5c2" "q-73751/selection/6d6811ceb4fb69a54ce1b24e6804e5f0148bafa1b76b847b06436eb966d36b67" "q-73751/selection/985f6b5ef1c8517ebf2244547e58da77a03c4a2e843c87009b203c6ea3c30ce0" "q-73751/selection/c16f73c6dcd2feff45d079ef404d7c8b47cf8f04221ee0cbcf38ede15c995ec9" "q-73751/selection/b281b0c65b28852a265e45d86efbe0f872541b03035b263e65e84f5f30e8f7a0"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-73751" :question/id #uuid "e4d5c647-074f-5eda-b4fd-fd73311149f0" :question/math-academy-id "q-73751" :question/problem "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}5x-10y=-5 \\\\ 2x-4y=2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form, and then find the general solution of the linear system." :question/worked-solution "First, we set up the augmented matrix for the system:\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}5 & -10 & -5 \\\\ 2 & -4 & 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nReducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}5 & -10 & -5 \\\\ 2 & -4 & 2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{5}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 2 & -4 & 2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x-2y=-1 \\\\ 0x+0y=4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHowever, the final equation $0x+0y=4$ has no solution. It simplifies to $0=4,$ which is a false statement.\n\nSo, there is no pair $x,y$ that satisfies both equations in the system. Consequently, the overall system has no solution." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-73751/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "07f2ae4c-ff07-5b99-a7b0-90f460081eef"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-73751"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-130922/selection/73604cf2443342adc2a738a87cfcb145375e964641d11a3e8c7ccb6894bc11df" :answer/id #uuid "6bf652d2-fa3b-5fdf-bb1d-6a8462c2431b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1-3y \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-130922/selection/c2245c2c50834f9c8753fe56bee708fa054955b52e09ea3b7a3d2be71d389b5b" :answer/id #uuid "1ccd5358-c0ab-5bea-b689-dc701eb72069" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-3y-1 \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-130922/selection/0e79abb073781ffa02cb54752834f6eac697f69f9b14b2cef695759af1c9c8a1" :answer/id #uuid "c9054393-30f1-5923-b32e-15ea3acad0ba" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}3y-1 \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-130922/selection/efd7ae29f5b95c11b30ee879de325058719a59e7c129276fdd54e966bae6e399" :answer/id #uuid "35b83e50-5a21-54e1-931d-7091856c0a0a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-y-3 \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-130922/selection/b323b85240321f69a79bc2229c178b05e61b8f6a1d1606818ca109abcc4d34f7" :answer/id #uuid "1382cad3-718b-55f0-a61e-4224134a2cd3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}y-3 \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-130922/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "e4871325-33a7-51eb-8af2-dcd6a6b97c80" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-130922/selection/c2245c2c50834f9c8753fe56bee708fa054955b52e09ea3b7a3d2be71d389b5b" :answer-field/choices ["q-130922/selection/73604cf2443342adc2a738a87cfcb145375e964641d11a3e8c7ccb6894bc11df" "q-130922/selection/c2245c2c50834f9c8753fe56bee708fa054955b52e09ea3b7a3d2be71d389b5b" "q-130922/selection/0e79abb073781ffa02cb54752834f6eac697f69f9b14b2cef695759af1c9c8a1" "q-130922/selection/efd7ae29f5b95c11b30ee879de325058719a59e7c129276fdd54e966bae6e399" "q-130922/selection/b323b85240321f69a79bc2229c178b05e61b8f6a1d1606818ca109abcc4d34f7"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-130922" :question/id #uuid "59028158-753f-502a-bd86-d054f28eae13" :question/math-academy-id "q-130922" :question/problem "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by \n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 9 & -3 \\\\ 2 & 6 & -2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce $M$ to row echelon form, and then find the general solution of the linear system represented by the matrix." :question/worked-solution "Reducing $M$ to echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & 9 & -3 \\\\ 2 & 6 & -2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 6 & -2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x+3y=-1 \\\\ 0x+0y=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince any pair of numbers $x,y$ is a solution of the final equation $0x+0y=0,$ we can remove this equation from the system. So, our system now consists of a single equation\n\n$$\nx+3y=-1.\n$$\n\nThe first variable $(x)$ is the basic variable, and the second variable $(y)$ is the free variable. Solving for the basic variable $(x)$ in terms of the free variable $(y),$ we get $x=-3y-1,$ and the general solution is\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=-3y-1 \\\\ y=y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $y$ is an arbitrary number. \n\nIn vector form, the general solution can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-3y-1 \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-130922/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "97cd9132-458b-5234-a3d2-22b633acb74c"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-130922"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
